00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,083
Let's work through this problem:

2
00:00:02,083 --> 00:00:03,333
Definite integral (FTC).

3
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:05,416
First we'll see the idea,

4
00:00:05,416 --> 00:00:06,666
then every step,

5
00:00:06,666 --> 00:00:09,240
each one checked by a computer.

6
00:00:09,766 --> 00:00:12,502
The definite integral adds up signed

7
00:00:12,502 --> 00:00:15,238
area under the curve between the limits.

8
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:16,666
Sum rule.

9
00:00:16,666 --> 00:00:18,401
Integrate term by term.

10
00:00:19,033 --> 00:00:20,283
Constant multiple rule.

11
00:00:20,283 --> 00:00:23,665
Pull the constant 3 out of the integral.

12
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:25,133
Power rule.

13
00:00:25,133 --> 00:00:31,412
∫ xⁿ dx = xⁿ⁺¹/(n + 1) with n = 2:

14
00:00:31,412 --> 00:00:37,692
raise the power by 1 and divide by the new power.

15
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:39,966
Integral of a constant.

16
00:00:39,966 --> 00:00:43,772
∫ c dx = c·x.

17
00:00:44,372 --> 00:00:44,788
Simplify.

18
00:00:44,788 --> 00:00:46,100
Combine the constants.

19
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:49,616
Fundamental Theorem: F(b) − F(a).

20
00:00:49,616 --> 00:00:52,778
Evaluate F at the top limit 2

21
00:00:52,778 --> 00:00:55,940
and subtract F at the bottom limit 0.

22
00:00:56,566 --> 00:00:56,983
Arithmetic.

23
00:00:56,983 --> 00:00:57,622
Simplify.

24
00:00:58,666 --> 00:01:00,802
So the answer is 10.

25
00:01:01,466 --> 00:01:06,466
Every step you just saw was checked by a computer algebra system,

26
00:01:06,466 --> 00:01:09,800
and the final answer was confirmed a second,

27
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:10,706
independent way.

28
00:01:11,166 --> 00:01:12,416
Find an antiderivative,

29
00:01:12,416 --> 00:01:14,916
evaluate it at the top limit,

30
00:01:14,916 --> 00:01:18,294
and subtract its value at the bottom limit.

31
